    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Augustus turned the war-torn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> into a monarchy in 27 BCE while keeping the Senate and consuls as a republican facade.</li><li>Its professional legions, 80,000 km of roads and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> bound a realm stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>.</li><li>The West fell gradually through civil war, Gothic and Vandal invasions and lost revenues, ending when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> in 476.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed the last Western emperor in 476, he simply sent the imperial regalia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and contemporaries barely remarked on it.</p></aside>
    </section>

